/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T06:46:25-07:00","id":860273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/853197-recs-for-kult?p=855355#post855355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Smart decision on their part. There are still too many elements of the game that smack of black metal grim darkness for my current tastes, but that's completely subjective and shouldn't affect how someone else might enjoy the game. My younger nihilistic self would probably like I though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> On that note: the cover art for Ophthalamia's (a very good, sadly under-appreciated Swedish BM band) A Jounrney in Darkness album (1994) is the same as the First Edition US cover art (1993). No idea if its a blatant steal, of if the cover artist worked for both, or what.<br /> <br /> Another &quot;it's a small world&quot; thing: Kult IP is, or was owned by Paradox Enterntainment, who used to be under one umbrella with paradox Ineractive, who have recently bought White Wolf.<br /> <br /> No idea if there is any overlap between the old Kult folks and the new WW folks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value"